{"term":"discern","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7d7ba8419290c90327","definition":"To detect with the senses, especially with the eyes.","example":"Meanwhile the brig had altered her tack, and was moving slowly to the east. Three hours later and the keenest eye could not have discerned her top-sails above the horizon.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["behold","see","spy","distinguish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discernability","discernable","discernance","discernible","discernment","indiscernible","misdiscern","undiscerned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be829359843300b9af","definition":"To perceive, recognize, or comprehend with the mind; to descry.","example":"If they discern any evidences of wrong-going in any direction that I have indicated, they will acknowledge that I had reason in what I wrote. If they discern no such thing, they will consider me altogether mistaken.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ken"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discernability","discernable","discernance","discernible","discernment","indiscernible","misdiscern","undiscerned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bee8cd590da19aacc9","definition":"To distinguish something as being different from something else; to differentiate or discriminate.","example":"He was too young to discern right from wrong.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["discriminate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["discernability","discernable","discernance","discernible","discernment","indiscernible","misdiscern","undiscerned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d6ee04c11e06fcb45","definition":"To perceive differences.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["behold","see","spy","distinguish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["discernability","discernable","discernance","discernible","discernment","indiscernible","misdiscern","undiscerned"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discern#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/dɪˈsɜːn/"},"wordFamily":["discernability","discernable","discernance","discernible","discernment","indiscernible","misdiscern","undiscerned"]}